<Placemark>   <name>Ahvenkoski Harbour</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>2</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 60.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 26.485<br />
                    Ancient Settlement in Kymenlaakos, Finland.<br/>Discovered in 2010.  A large harbor, dating from around 1000–1200 AD at the mouth of western branch of the Kymijoki River in Finland. Findings include...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=34963" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_g</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>26.485,60.5,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Järvensuo I</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>3</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 61.33209 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 23.95069<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Finland/thumb/figure204_final.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    The wetland site of Järvensuo 1 in south-west Finland was a chance discovery during the digging of a ditch in the 1950s. The discovery, in 2020, of a unique wooden snake figurine broadens the underst...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=55465" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>23.95069,61.33209,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Kierikki Keskus</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Ancient Village or Settlement <b>Alt Name:</b> Kierikkikangas Stone Age Excavations <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>5</b> Condition: <b>2</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 65.359466 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 26.05957<br />
                    Ancient Village or Settlement in Yli-Ii, Finland. Ancient settlement northern banks of the river Iijoki dating to about 4000-3500 BCE. A wooden pathway to the Stone Age village goes through the site.<...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=20018" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#2_g</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>26.05957,65.359466,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark></Folder><Folder><name><![CDATA[Artificial Mound]]></name><open>0</open>
<Placemark>   <name>Björkens/Söderskog</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Artificial Mound <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>4</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 60.2198 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 19.98319<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Finland/thumb/7_-_Björkens-Söderskog_VII_-_Ship_barrow.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Artificial Mound in Finland. 39 graves from Late Iron-Age. In the burial field, there are several types of burial facilities that are characteristic of the Late Iron Age, including three ship barrows ...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
		     <a href="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=57723" >Link To More Information</a><br />
                    ]]></description>    <styleUrl>#3_r</styleUrl>   <Point>     <coordinates>19.98319,60.2198,0</coordinates>   </Point>  </Placemark>
<Placemark>   <name>Flyhagen/Knösäkern</name>   <description><![CDATA[
        <b>Type:</b> Artificial Mound <b>Alt Name:</b> Kungshögarna <br /> Pos Accuracy: <b>4</b> Condition: <b>4</b> (5 is best)   Ambience: <b>4</b>  Access: <b>4</b>  (5 is best)<br />
                    <b>Lat:</b> 60.23034 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b>Long</b>: 19.99339<img src="http://www.megalithic.co.uk/a558/a312/gallery/Scandinavia/Finland/thumb/1_-_Flyhagen-Knösäkern_I_-_Mound.jpg" align="right" valign="top"></a>
<br />
                    Artificial Mound in Finland. 37 graves from Late Iron Age. Exposed location next to plantations, damaged by these. On the burial ground are some of Åland's largest burial facilities from the Late Iro...<b>.</b> (c) Meg. Portal contributors.<br />
